# Verification Checklist

Run this before merging any code that is wired to an external API, package, or service.

## Checklist

- [ ] Tests pass (`pytest` / `npm test` / equivalent)
- [ ] Linter passes — no new errors introduced
- [ ] All imports resolve — no hallucinated packages or methods
- [ ] API endpoints actually exist — verified against live docs or source
- [ ] Behavior matches the spec — not just "code looks right"
- [ ] Edge cases covered: empty input, null/None, large data, concurrent access, timezone differences
- [ ] No secrets or API keys hardcoded — use env vars
- [ ] `console.log` / debug prints removed from production paths

## Gotcha Log

Document every time the agent produces incorrect code. Add patterns here as they emerge.

| Pattern | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| Hallucinated import | Agent used a function that doesn't exist in the installed version |
| Silent catch | `except Exception: pass` or empty `catch {}` swallowing real errors |
| Wrong HTTP method | Agent called POST where the API expects PUT, or vice versa |
| Missing await | Async function called without `await`, returns Promise instead of value |
